# Getting started skill

A **workbook** is the woven artifact the `work` CLI compiles from a folder of `.work`
files — literate documents where prose narrates and `do … end` blocks run. You author
`.work` (no HTML, no code fences); the CLI weaves the folder into the workbook and
ships it. Start here to learn the model, the file format, and the CLI verbs before
authoring anything.

When the user wants to make or ship a workbook, read the references below in order —
they take you from "what is a workbook" to running the `work` CLI.

app :getting_started do
  title       "Getting started with Workbooks"
  description "Author and ship .work workbooks. Use when starting a new workbook, learning the .work format, or onboarding to the work CLI."

  section "The model" do
    page "introduction/what-is-a-workbook"
    page "introduction/what-is-a-work-file"
  end

  section "The work CLI" do
    page "introduction/what-is-the-work-cli"
    page "tooling/get-started-with-your-cli-agent"
  end
end
